[{:db/id 17592186341929 :question/problem "![](images/1f/1f2d8b9faac6c300b41902cea5065bf8bafb02c137232ee79779a4dc3ff67f33.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n\nII. The function is differentiable at $x=1$\n\nIII. The function is continuous at $x=2$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186341928 :question/problem "![](images/a8/a8a70a2f28585b63d2a083b42eb6ad54bfb581b5f13c699a3bc3c8d836afaee8.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The function is continuous at $x=1$\n\nII. The function is continuous at $x=0$\n\nIII. The function is differentiable at $x=0$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186237867 :question/problem "Given that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$, has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$, and is differentiable at $x=-1$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nI. It is differentiable at $x=0$\n\nII. It  is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n\nIII. It is continuous at $x=-1$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329826 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+1, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 3, & x=1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nI. It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\nII. It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n\nIII. It is differentiable on the interval $(-1,2)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
